{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"0c9a4fa8075606641249beca57e588dd61cbba2d5ffcb532b82457c0db5bef98","digest":{"component_or_area":"Pass-1 chunk and agent pool","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py:438,462-464","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py:184-232","CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS","tests/llm/test_pass1_warmup.py","tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_warmup.py","coverage.batch_plan","LLMUnavailableError"],"problem_keywords":["cache efficiency","warm-then-fan-out","token usage","concurrent llm calls","plan prefix caching","redundant cache writes"],"propositions":["Pass-1 submits all chunks and agent futures concurrently to a 6-wide pool, causing redundant cache writes of the shared plan-bearing system prefix when the cache is cold, consuming ~3.7x more tokens than ideal","The warm-then-fan-out pattern reduces redundant prefix cache writes by running a single call serially first to populate the cache, then fanning out the remainder to the pool in parallel","The warm gate is triggered when estimated shared-prefix tokens exceed CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS and there are >= 2 Pass-1 calls; below these thresholds or with a single call, behavior is unchanged","Non-systemic failures during the warm call degrade gracefully to direct fan-out of all remaining calls, preserving review completion"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787496865601001001,"uuid":"eb58d303-bc2f-4dcd-9d46-1751a43562ec"}